  },
  data: {
    LLM: "1. Deal: five cards face down to each player and five face down to the table. 2. Players look at their hands. 3. Dealer turns the table cards face up one at a time; after each card is turned there is a round of betting (check, bet, call, raise, or fold). 4. After the fifth and final betting round, showdown: each active player's hand is the best five-card hand from any combination of their hole cards and the five table cards. 5. Highest hand wins the pot.",
    Player: "1. Deal: five cards face down to each player and five face down to the table. 2. Players look at their hands. 3. Dealer turns the table cards face up one at a time; after each card is turned there is a round of betting (check, bet, call, raise, or fold). 4. After the fifth and final betting round, showdown: each active player's hand is the best five-card hand from any combination of their hole cards and the five table cards. 5. Highest hand wins the pot.",
    objective: 'Win the pot by having the highest five-card poker hand, formed from any combination of your five hole cards and the five community cards.',
    gameplay: "1. Deal: five cards face down to each player and five face down to the table. 2. Players look at their hands. 3. Dealer turns the table cards face up one at a time; after each card is turned there is a round of betting (check, bet, call, raise, or fold). 4. After the fifth and final betting round, showdown: each active player's hand is the best five-card hand from any combination of their hole cards and the five table cards. 5. Highest hand wins the pot.",
    keyRules: [
      'Each player has five hole cards; five community cards are revealed one by one with a betting round after each.',
      "Best five-card hand uses any combination of the player's five hole cards and the five community cards.",
      'Standard poker hand rankings determine the winner; standard betting order applies (e.g. check, bet, call, raise, fold).',
